{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s33-p01",
      "text": "We use pencils to write and erasers to erase what we've written.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p02",
      "text": "But no one knows who invented the pencil or when it was invented.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p03",
      "text": "The Swiss Conrad Gesner described a pencil in a book in 1565.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p04",
      "text": "Mr Gesner said it was a piece of wood or bamboo with lead inside it.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p04.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p05",
      "text": "Pencils weren't popular, and people continued to write with pens.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p06",
      "text": "They used bird feathers as pens.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p06.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p07",
      "text": "Then, in 1795, some pioneers founded the pencil industry when they started making pencils from graphite chips, and pencils became very popular.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p08",
      "text": "One pencil can make a line as long as 55 kilometres.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p09",
      "text": "People then used pens with metal points.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p10",
      "text": "They had to dip the point into ink after every few letters.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p10.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p10.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p11",
      "text": "Next, someone invented a fountain pen that could hold ink inside.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p12",
      "text": "A fountain pen can write several pages before you have to fill it again.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p12.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p12.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p13",
      "text": "Nowadays, there are purple or silver inks that allow you to write in fancy colours.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p14",
      "text": "Two brothers, Ladislao and Georg Biro, invented the ballpoint pen.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p15",
      "text": "Pilots liked the pens.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p15.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p16",
      "text": "They couldn't write with fountain pens in planes because the ink leaked out.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p17-01",
      "text": "Some of today's ballpoint pens have a spring inside,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p17-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p17-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p17-02",
      "text": "so that you can hide the point when you are not writing.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p17-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p17-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p18",
      "text": "Companies use colourful packs, maybe printed with cute animals like rabbits or giraffes, to attract customers.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p18.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p18.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33-p19",
      "text": "Whatever they look like, we see them everywhere on sale and use them every day.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p19.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s33-p19.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
